You are given two strings word1 and word2. Merge the strings by adding letters in alternating order, starting with word1. If a string is longer than the other, append the
additional letters onto the end of the merged string.Return the merged string.
Example 1:

Input: word1 = "abc", word2 = "pqr"
Output: "apbqcr"
Explanation: The merged string will be merged as so:
word1:  a   b   c
word2:    p   q   r
merged: a p b q c r
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
class Solution:
    def mergeAlternately(self, word1: str, word2: str) -> str:
      merged=""
      len1,len2=len(word1),len(word2)
      for i in range(max(len1,len2)):
        if i < len1:
            merged+=word1[i]
        if i < len2:
            merged+=word2[i]
      return merged
